  "decisionPolicy": {
    "highConfidence": "At least two independent evidence groups support the same type, the room-boundary association is valid, and no high-impact contradiction remains.",
    "mediumConfidence": "Evidence is plausible but incomplete; keep the candidate and list missing evidence.",
    "lowConfidence": "Only one weak cue, ambiguous symbol, or no stable room boundary; keep type unknown and request review.",
    "conflict": "If strong evidence supports incompatible types, first test whether geometry incorrectly merges adjacent spaces; do not average away the conflict.",
    "noText": "Use the same inference process without text labels; do not substitute layout-count guesses for visual evidence.",
    "negativeEvidence": "Absence of a fixture only lowers confidence when image resolution and detector recall are known to be adequate.",
    "experienceUpdate": "A reviewed correction becomes a versioned case with source crop, evidence, previous prediction, corrected type/boundary, rationale, and regression assertion."
